# HB Briefing - Default Intelligence Feeds
# Add one RSS or Atom feed URL per line. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Two kinds of source:
#   * direct  - the publisher's own feed. Fetchable, so stage 2 deep reads work.
#   * query   - a Google News search. Used where no usable feed exists, but item
#               links are encrypted redirects, so deep reads cannot follow them.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Regulators (direct)

# Federal Trade Commission (FTC) consumer protection & press releases
https://www.ftc.gov/feeds/press-release-consumer-protection.xml

# Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) newsroom
https://www.consumerfinance.gov/about-us/newsroom/feed/

# CFPB enforcement actions - dockets, consent orders, penalties
https://www.consumerfinance.gov/enforcement/actions/feed/

# Securities and Exchange Commission press releases - enforcement outcomes
https://www.sec.gov/news/pressreleases.rss

# Federal Register: FCC final and proposed rules only. The unfiltered agency feed is
# mostly procedural notices (information collections), which drown the digest.
https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents.rss?conditions%5Bagencies%5D%5B%5D=federal-communications-commission&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=RULE&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRORULE&order=newest

# Federal Register: FTC final and proposed rules only
https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents.rss?conditions%5Bagencies%5D%5B%5D=federal-trade-commission&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=RULE&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRORULE&order=newest

# ------------------------------------------------------- Trade press (direct)
# Direct publisher feeds; unlike the queries below these are readable end to end.

# Broadband Breakfast - US broadband policy and regulation
https://broadbandbreakfast.com/feed/

# Telecompetitor - US ISP market, regulation and deal coverage.
# Its own feed sits behind a Cloudflare bot filter that refuses every automated
# client (HTTP 403), so it is reached through Google News instead. Deep reads still
# work: the redirect is resolved to the publisher URL before the article is fetched.
https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=site%3Atelecompetitor.com&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en

# ------------------------------------------------- World and business news (optional)
# Major outlets that publish working RSS/Atom feeds, each verified reachable and current.
# They are commented out because the default profile is deliberately narrow: a dozen
# general-news feeds would add hundreds of items to every scan. Uncomment the URL lines
# you want, or start from profiles/general_news.json, which is built for this.
#
# Checked and *not* included: Reuters retired public RSS (404); AP and USA Today refuse
# automated clients (403/402); CNN's edition feed and the WSJ world feed still resolve but
# have stopped publishing.

# World
# BBC News (world)
# https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/world/rss.xml
# BBC News (top stories)
# https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/rss.xml
# The Guardian (world)
# https://www.theguardian.com/world/rss
# The Guardian (business)
# https://www.theguardian.com/uk/business/rss
